  "note": "The revision of each specification that zod-nostr's schemas are written against. `sources` names each document family and its repository, `documents` holds that family's entries under the same key, and `commit` identifies a revision in that repository and `date` is when it landed there \u2014 the commit's committer date, which is not always the author date a commit page shows; neither is the date zod-nostr looked at it. `sha256` is the SHA-256 of the document's Markdown at that commit, so a checker can detect when the upstream text changes. An entry is bumped when the document is re-read and the schemas are confirmed against it \u2014 git history and CHANGELOG.md record when that happened. `npm run test:spec-baseline` keeps this file and the spec modules under src/ from disagreeing.",
